Added the flow session: a signed cookie holding the pending authorization attempts, keyed from `plone.keyring` the way `plone.session` keys its auth tickets. Plone 6.2 ships no `session_data_manager`, and an unsigned cookie would let an attacker author their own `state`, PKCE verifier and nonce, which is exactly the binding the callback depends on. The signing key is derived from the ring rather than used directly, and every key in the ring is accepted on verification so a rotation does not strand a login in flight. @ericof
